// The card's two faces, carried in the repository as bytes.
//
// TWO FINDINGS ARE BUILT INTO THIS FILE AND BOTH COST A PRODUCTION FAILURE.
//
// 1. Font fallback is silent. A missing face does not throw and does not warn.
//    On the first real render the honorific came out as an empty gap in a
//    sentence about the Prophet, peace be upon him, and nothing reported it.
//
// 2. Worse: a LOCAL test can pass for the wrong reason. The first version of
//    this shipped a face called "DejaVu Sans" and rendered perfectly here,
//    because this machine has DejaVu Sans installed system wide, so the system
//    copy was quietly doing the drawing. Vercel has no system fonts. The card
//    went out completely blank: border, gradient, not one letter.
//
//    So the family is called NoorCard, a name NO system font anywhere can
//    satisfy. If the embedded faces are not loaded, the card is blank and the
//    failure is loud, on any machine, instead of being masked by a lucky one.
//    tests/card.mjs asserts the name is not a real font's name.
//
// Built by scripts/gen-card-fonts.py from DejaVu Sans (Bitstream Vera licence,
// free to use and redistribute), subset to the characters the library actually
// contains, and renamed. Re-run it after adding cards in a new language.

